Why this design is safe and meets requirements
•	MCP tools call IBankingService (existing application layer). BankingService enforces ownership by calling ICurrentUserAccessor.GetCurrentCustomerIdAsync(); it performs resource checks against CustomerId derived from a server-side session. The MCP layer does not add or accept customer identity parameters; resource selectors (accountId, loanId, cardId) are accepted but ownership is enforced server-side.
•	The MCP server does not query the database directly for LLM input; it calls the service layer which performs necessary checks and mapping to safe DTOs.
•	Sensitive values are not exposed: session tokens are only used server-side, DTOs do not contain PINs or full card numbers.
•	Error handling avoids leaking internal details (stack traces / SQL exceptions).
