How MCP obtains authenticated CustomerId
•	The MCP server is an ASP.NET Core Web app that accepts requests (e.g., from a validated LLM runtime or other server). It reads the NB_SID cookie from the incoming request (IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext.Request.Cookies). The CurrentUserAccessor hashes the raw token, looks up CustomerSessions in the database, validates expiry and revoked state, and returns session.CustomerId. This is the authoritative customer identity used by the BankingService.
How ownership is enforced
•	BankingService (existing) calls ICurrentUserAccessor.GetCurrentCustomerIdAsync() and filters or rejects resources if they do not belong to the authenticated customer. The MCP tools call BankingService methods only — ownership enforcement is preserved in the same place as the primary API.
How MCP server is hosted
•	NovaBanking.McpServer is a normal ASP.NET Core Web app (Program.cs). It hosts endpoints under /mcp/Tools for the MCP toolset. It shares the same infrastructure project for DbContext and uses the same session table and token hashing logic.
