Architectural limitations / notes
•	This MCP server expects to receive the same NB_SID cookie used by the API. For native LLM integrations, the runtime calling the MCP endpoints must present an authenticated server-side session cookie (NB_SID) for the target customer. The MCP server relies on standard HTTP cookie transport and server-side session validation. If an external LLM runtime cannot securely provide the NB_SID cookie in requests, a secure bridge is required (for example, a server-side component that performs user authentication, obtains an NB_SID session, and calls MCP tools on behalf of authenticated users). Do not accept CustomerId in MCP requests to bypass authentication—this is enforced in code and tests.
